# Copy to frontend/.env.local (local) or set in Vercel > Settings > Environment Variables.
# All of these are server-only: none starts with NEXT_PUBLIC_, so the browser never sees them.
# The search route uses the first option that's configured:

# 1) A separately deployed Python/FastAPI recommendation service.
# RECOMMENDATION_API_URL=https://buybyfit-api.example.com

# 2) The real catalogue in Supabase, over its REST API (semantic search via the match_products
#    pgvector function, plus real product pages). Use the project's *publishable* (anon) key from
#    Supabase > Project Settings > API; row-level security makes it read-only.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_replace_me

# Optional: where the compressed AR models (/models/*.glb) are hosted, e.g. the ar-mvp server or a
# storage bucket. Without it, product cards don't offer AR.
# AR_ASSET_BASE_URL=https://your-ar-host.example.com

# Optional: "fp32" for exact query vectors (larger model download); default "q8" (cosine 0.997).
# EMBEDDING_DTYPE=q8

# 3) Neither set: the built-in fictional demo catalogue.
